---
import MainLayout2 from "../../layouts/mainlayout2.astro";

const SITE_TITLE = "Stephen — About";
const SITE_DESCRIPTION = "A personal introduction, beyond the resume.";
---

<MainLayout2
  title={SITE_TITLE}
  description={SITE_DESCRIPTION}
  activeNav="about"
  pageTitle="About"
  pageDescription="A personal introduction, beyond the resume."
>
  <section class="about-grid">
    <article class="prose">
      <p>
        I have always been drawn to understanding how things fit together,
        whether it is the structure of a city, the flow of data, or the logic
        behind a crossword puzzle. My background winds through geoscience,
        economics, and policy, from studying Earth systems at Penn State to
        exploring spatial and environmental economics at Vrije Universiteit
        Amsterdam. Somewhere between field maps and regression models,
        I realized that I am happiest when I am uncovering patterns and
        turning them into something practical.
      </p>

      <p>
        That curiosity eventually led me into work focused on energy,
        infrastructure, and governance, including projects that supported
        the U.S. Department of State’s engagement with Greenland and
        contributions to U.S. Department of Energy oil and gas publications.
        The common thread across all of it is investigation: digging into
        complex systems, finding what matters, and writing clearly enough
        that others can act on it. I believe that good analysis should not
        merely live in spreadsheets (and I do love a good spreadsheet);
        it should tell a story that moves our understanding forward.
      </p>

      <p>
        Outside of work, I channel that same mix of curiosity and focus
        into other things. I cook and am slowly filling my own handwritten
        cookbook. I read often and am currently reading
        <em>Children of Dune</em>. I also enjoy playing strategy games that
        require at least three cups of coffee and a long attention span.
        I travel whenever I can, exercise to clear my mind, and I still
        complete the <em>Wall Street Journal</em> crossword almost every
        morning, a ritual that combines both discipline and stubbornness.
      </p>

      <p>
        If there is a theme to all of it, it is that I like challenges
        that do not have obvious answers. Whether it is a dataset,
        a recipe, or a new city, I continue until I understand how it
        works and, if possible, make it a little better by the time
        I am finished.
      </p>
    </article>

    <aside class="facts">
      <h3>Quick facts</h3>

      <ul>
        <li><strong>Currently reading:</strong> Children of Dune</li>
        <li><strong>Morning ritual:</strong> Wall Street Journal and its crossword</li>
        <li><strong>Hobbies:</strong> Cooking, travel, strategy games</li>
        <li><strong>Previously:</strong> Spatial and Applied Economics at VU Amsterdam</li>
        <li><strong>Focus areas:</strong> Energy, infrastructure, governance, and writing</li>
      </ul>
    </aside>
  </section>

  <style>
    .about-grid {
      display: grid;
      gap: 26px;
    }

    @media (min-width: 1024px) {
      .about-grid {
        grid-template-columns: minmax(420px, 75ch) 1fr;
      }
    }

    .prose {
      max-width: 75ch;
      font-size: 1rem;
      color: var(--text, #0f141b);
    }

    .prose p {
      margin: 0 0 14px;
      color: inherit;
    }

    .prose strong {
      font-weight: 700;
      color: var(--title, #111827);
    }

    .prose em {
      color: inherit;
    }

    .prose a {
      word-break: break-word;
      color: var(--accent, #0a67ff);
    }

    .facts {
      border: 1px solid var(--border, #e5e7eb);
      border-radius: 14px;
      padding: 14px;
      background: var(--surface, #ffffff);
      color: var(--text, #0f141b);
      align-self: start;
    }

    .facts h3 {
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      font-family: "Playfair Display", Georgia, serif;
      font-size: 1.15rem;
      color: var(--title, #111827);
    }

    .facts ul {
      list-style: none;
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0;
      display: grid;
      gap: 8px;
    }

    .facts li {
      font-size: 0.95rem;
      color: var(--text-soft, #374151);
    }

    .facts strong {
      color: var(--title, #111827);
    }
  </style>
</MainLayout2>